steps.body:
Kotlin has no `static` keyword. Class-level members go in a **companion object**:

```kotlin
class User private constructor(val name: String) {
    companion object {
        const val MAX_NAME = 50
        fun create(name: String) = User(name.take(MAX_NAME))
    }
}

val u = User.create("Ann")
```

You call members through the class name, like statics. A private constructor plus a factory in the companion is a common pattern.

